title One program, many tool calls

model    "Model"
runcode  "run_code tool"
process  "Program process"
checks   "Tool checks"
readtool "read tool"
calls    "Tool calls" counter 0

model -> runcode -> process -> checks -> readtool

program at model

# Counting lines in 40 files would take 41 steps one call at a time.
pause "Here the model writes one program instead."

# The model sends the program, and the harness starts a process for it.
program -> runcode "The model sees only run_code; other tools are functions in the program."
program -> process : running "The program runs in its own Node process."

# A tool call leaves the program and passes the same checks as a direct call.
new call1 at process
call1 -> checks : waiting "Pre-execute and approval run as for any call."
call1 -> readtool : running
calls +1
call1 -> process : done "The file text goes back to the program, not to the model."
remove call1

# The loop repeats inside the program; the model is not asked again.
calls = 41 "glob once, then read 40 times."

# Only the returned value reaches the model.
program : done
new answer at process
answer -> model 1200ms "files: 40, total: 3120 is about 10 tokens."
remove program
